54ca09d0f54b3ff3d58374dc152bb.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:50PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Friday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 9:43PM MDT until October 23 at 9:45AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\nLow-water crossings are inundated with water and may not be\npassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 942 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in\nthe warned area.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nSpecie Creek, San Miguel River, and South Fork San Miguel River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMountain Village, Sawpit, Fall Creek and Placerville.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T09:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"San Miguel, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c404575618305aa082398d6d4504891602739aa0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c404575618305aa082398d6d4504891602739aa0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T05:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 230552 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1152 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Several creeks, streams, and rivers have already reached flood stage due to persistent rainfall, and modeled responses suggest several others will do the same overnight. - Impacts from high water levels and flooding may be seen throughout Friday. - A few ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-232200- Little Snake Forecast Ar